{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1121231-banality-as-trait-of-action","id":1121231,"title":"Banality as trait of action","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-27T02:16:35-07:00","id":1121231,"title":"Banality as trait of action","content":"Recently I had this weird idea about banality...<br /> <br /> First I thought to get rid of Banality of places (and yes, canonically, there was at least one place, defined as Banal Black Hole - in 2ed Immortal Eyes San Francisco supplement). <br /> There is no intrinsic Banality score of the place. <br /> <br /> Then I thought why not also get rid of Splats' Banality score. For each their own.<br /> There might be Dreamers Technocracy, although brainwashing definitely can mess with that. <br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking... What if Banality has no Intrinsic score and depends solely on two concepts. Behavior and performative action and various B. scores only belong to continuous preformative actions and massive events.<br /> <br /> Boring office wage slave non-entity function of a human on their job in broad daylight behind their desk is most banal thing you could imagine. You know it. They know it. But let them out of that place and they might shine brightly wuth their individuality. That makes most people dagerous in most situations, unless they're off their leash. When they're most themselves, most genuine, not a role they were put to play. <br /> <br /> The danger of Autumn People, is that they let Banality of their life to poison their thoughts and spread into every facet of their life. And they can teach or force other to behave that way, if for a time.<br /> <br /> Accordingly, older Changelings can't just lower their Banality, unless they plan to act, like Childlings or creatures of pure Dreaming and whimsy.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:20:20-07:00","id":1121369,"title":"","content":"This &quot;shining brightly&quot; is the moment when a changeling might awaken a dreamer. But ultimately, you have to see the bigger picture: That guy who is a drone during the day but let's say LARPs once a month. He is still banality 7-8, He has a fixed place where he lets out the bit of spark that he has. He will probably never write that novel he was thinking about. He will most likely save his money for worse times instead of going on that trip to a foreign country. It's a changeling's life to cut them free.<br /> As for Technocracy... no. Their mindset is based on the idea that you don't exist. You are a random deviation from a perfect reality that has to be fixed. If even one of them goes away from that, their Psych Ops will fix them. Even when they have a break through in their fields, they probably go down to 8 at best (and even then, they get stink-eye for being so rambunctious. NOW DO A TEST GROUP! AND AGAIN!)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T18:50:16-07:00","id":1121660,"title":"","content":"Control isn't omnipresent. Most Technocratic Mages have all sorts of thoughts that contradict Control, they're just not stupid enough to let Control know about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T22:09:33-07:00","id":1121715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Davesknd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1121231-banality-as-trait-of-action?p=1121369#post1121369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This &amp;quot;shining brightly&amp;quot; is the moment when a changeling might awaken a dreamer. But ultimately, you have to see the bigger picture: That guy who is a drone during the day but let's say LARPs once a month. He is still banality 7-8, He has a fixed place where he lets out the bit of spark that he has. He will probably never write that novel he was thinking about. He will most likely save his money for worse times instead of going on that trip to a foreign country. It's a changeling's life to cut them free.<br /> As for Technocracy... no. Their mindset is based on the idea that you don't exist. You are a random deviation from a perfect reality that has to be fixed. If even one of them goes away from that, their Psych Ops will fix them. Even when they have a break through in their fields, they probably go down to 8 at best (and even then, they get stink-eye for being so rambunctious. NOW DO A TEST GROUP! AND AGAIN!)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a splat and it's either based on superficial stereotyping or kind of omniscience we humans don't have. <br /> <br /> Also, lumping people into groups like that is very easy and useful. <br /> <br /> So, what if the drone-LARPer you mentioned spends money on charity instead and has ongoing depression and that larping experience in about once a month is the only thing, that makes them happy and alive, but they can't kinda just drop their job. Are they &quot;secretly a good guys&quot; now or they just pretend to be more creative and wondrous, than they are?<br /> <br /> How about a doctor, that has to deal with human suffering to much, that she shuts down her feelings almost completely do to her work properly, (yes, exactly as lifeless and drone-like, as you can imagine) only allowing to express her personality with dark, dry humour during breaks? It's never so simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T01:36:49-07:00","id":1121753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1121231-banality-as-trait-of-action?p=1121715#post1121715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, what if the drone-LARPer you mentioned spends money on charity instead and has ongoing depression and that larping experience in about once a month is the only thing, that makes them happy and alive, but they can't kinda just drop their job. Are they &quot;secretly a good guys&quot; now or they just pretend to be more creative and wondrous, than they are?<br /> <br /> How about a doctor, that has to deal with human suffering to much, that she shuts down her feelings almost completely do to her work properly, (yes, exactly as lifeless and drone-like, as you can imagine) only allowing to express her personality with dark, dry humour during breaks? It's never so simple.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are conflating Glamour with kindness. Glamour isn't about being good and decent, it's about creativity. Someone who designs and tests torture devices will be less banal than someone who stands in the kitchen of a homeless shelter and mechanically cooks soup. Same with your doctor. It they don't feel a spark of creative joy during their deeds, they are not producing Glamour. If you have a literal serial killer who kidnaps people, tortures then an then makes soup bowls out of their skullcaps, you have one low banality individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T11:56:51-07:00","id":1121985,"title":"","content":"Anyway, I got your point. <br /> <br /> Without going further off topic I'd prefer hear other's thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}